tion': 'A section list contains a null element; the method should not silently ignore it and must propagate the NPE caused by invoking rec.toWire on a null reference.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'out', 'value': 'mocked DNSOutput'}], 'expected': 'Header.toWire(out) is invoked once; RecordA.toWire(out, 1, compression) is invoked once; RecordB is null and is skipped without exception.', 'description': 'A section list contains a mix of a valid Record and a null element; the method should invoke toWire on the valid Record and ignore the null entry, not throwing an exception.'}]}, {'group': 'Message.toWire(DNSOutput) - order of header and records', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'out', 'value': 'mocked DNSOutput'}], 'expected': 'Header.toWire(out) is invoked before any Record.toWire; verification using InOrder confirms header call precedes RecordX and RecordY calls.', 'description': 'Ensures that the header serialization occurs prior to serializing any records, regardless of how many sections are present.'}]}, {'group': 'Message.toWire(DNSOutput) - separate Compression instances per call', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'out', 'value': 'mocked DNSOutput'}], 'expected': 'Two consecutive calls to Message.toWire(out) each create a distinct Compression object; the Compression instance used in the first call is not the same (by reference) as the one used in the second call.', 'description': 'Verifies that the method does not retain a static or cached Compression object across separate invocations, which could corrupt name compression state.'}]}, {'group': 'Message.toWire(DNSOutput) - zero‑length sections array', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'out', 'value': 'mocked DNSOutput'}], 'expected': 'Header.toWire(out) is invoked once; no Record.toWire is invoked because sections.length == 0, therefore the outer loop never executes.', 'description': 'Tests the edge case where the Message is constructed with an empty sections array (length 0). The method should handle it gr